				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:30:09.079Z",
			"content": "<p>I’M INTERESTED</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzxyvq6sk2q",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzxx6qfdc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mdh2.bsky.social/post/3ljzxyvq6sk2q",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:30:32.839Z",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzxzs4edc2y",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzxx6qfdc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3ljzxzs4edc2y",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:31:02.602Z",
			"content": "<p>ah no need to apologize! just trying to understand the context — thank you!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzy6ptvss2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzwqny4m22v",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com/post/3ljzy6ptvss2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Patrick Brosset",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/bafkreicsgx4oaqbtatg44m557fqinh4zp2e4evaxpqm6rjg65o4vsawrnq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:33:48.000Z",
			"content": "<p>We're definitely interested in talking more about this on the WebDX CG. Progressive enhancements, polyfills, and accessibility have come up multiple times in the past. So far, we've not been able to incorporate these aspects into Baseline calculation though. But I do believe we should.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyhkr7uk2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzy6ptvss2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com/post/3ljzyhkr7uk2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Patrick Brosset",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/bafkreicsgx4oaqbtatg44m557fqinh4zp2e4evaxpqm6rjg65o4vsawrnq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:38:44.658Z",
			"content": "<p>One of the things I've tried to steer the group towards in the first years of the project is to avoid \"hiding\" things that are not yet supported. Anything we can do to make features easier to discover/use, not harder, is valuable.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyjiprbk2d",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me/post/3ljzyjiprbk2d",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andy Davies",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/bafkreibthta5fiablcbztoiuclttohjox4ilrok6eex2qd42sxvgrhzuny"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:39:49.623Z",
			"content": "<p>Got to admit I still tend to go to Can I Use</p>\n<p>Not quite sure why we needed another alternative</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyrqnspk2u",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzvytozis2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org/post/3ljzyrqnspk2u",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stuart Langridge",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/bafkreiakpmfei5j6asycfke34nwmb2l2lbw42wg22bic7m5azmii64iflq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:44:26.382Z",
			"content": "<p>\"Baseline Newly Available\" is useless. It means \"someone somewhere thought of this. It's not everywhere. Don't use it.\" It is extremely annoying that it was invented, and afaict it was invented because people were sad that their new feature was not yet \"baseline\" and so people wouldn't use it.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzytv5oec2u",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyrqnspk2u",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org/post/3ljzytv5oec2u",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stuart Langridge",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/bafkreiakpmfei5j6asycfke34nwmb2l2lbw42wg22bic7m5azmii64iflq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T16:45:38.205Z",
			"content": "<p>this is harsher than I normally am about stuff. But I was super annoyed at \"newly available\". It was Really Useful to explain to teams I work with that \"if a thing says 'baseline' it's probably OK for us, otherwise don't\" and now there's a special new baseline which utterly invalidates that.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzrr4udc2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyjiprbk2d",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3ljzzrr4udc2s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:02:20.618Z",
			"content": "<p>I see the value in a simplified goalpost for features (for developers) but I think most of the benefit is in cross-browser planning — features categorized by aspirational support</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzsqyty22s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyhkr7uk2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3ljzzsqyty22s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:02:54.040Z",
			"content": "<p>interesting! “hiding” in what view?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzvoyxqk2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzytv5oec2u",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3ljzzvoyxqk2s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:04:32.611Z",
			"content": "<p>I think that’s fair feedback. I’m not sure the arbitrary 30 month goalpost is a good finish line for “Widely available”&nbsp;either — hmm</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzvsrys22o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzsqyty22s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com/post/3ljzzvsrys22o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Patrick Brosset",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/bafkreicsgx4oaqbtatg44m557fqinh4zp2e4evaxpqm6rjg65o4vsawrnq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:04:36.577Z",
			"content": "<p>As in, Baseline comes with the risk of hiding too many features from the web: those that aren't supported across browsers even though they're perfectly fine to use.<br>\nShowing a \"Limited\" Baseline banner on a doc website about a given feature comes with the risk of steering people away from it.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk223bfpgk2u",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzvoyxqk2s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org/post/3lk223bfpgk2u",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stuart Langridge",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sil.kryogenix.org",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/bafkreiakpmfei5j6asycfke34nwmb2l2lbw42wg22bic7m5azmii64iflq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:07:39.675Z",
			"content": "<p>I think that's OK, myself (which is why I liked \"baseline\"). It's essentially a more formal definition for the oft-used and not-well-defined \"this requires a modern browser\", I think</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk227qxt5k25",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:y52xi2qdwcfsjkrno3aykkhc/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk223bfpgk2u",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lk227qxt5k25",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:10:10.215Z",
			"content": "<p>ah, that phrase sets off red flags for me but I see your point 😅</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk22hvr3y225",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzzvsrys22o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lk22hvr3y225",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:14:43.673Z",
			"content": "<p>Ah, I see — yeah. That dovetails back to Baseline missing some pieces if you want to encourage or discourage usage on a feature, imo! “Limited but safe!”</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk22naoqcc2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk22hvr3y225",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com/post/3lk22naoqcc2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Patrick Brosset",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/patrickbrosset.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/bafkreicsgx4oaqbtatg44m557fqinh4zp2e4evaxpqm6rjg65o4vsawrnq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:17:42.902Z",
			"content": "<p>Filed <a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/2758\">github.com/web-platform...</a> to put it on our radar. We'll likely discuss at our next CG meeting (which you're more than welcome to join, details here: <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/community/webdx/\">www.w3.org/community/we...</a>), but please feel free to comment on the issue too.<br>\nPinging <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:bm5d7drix5fs77sx44xbpyww\">@miriam.codes</a> who had made a similar point too.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk237lmc2s26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzxx6qfdc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social/post/3lk237lmc2s26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mary Branscombe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/bafkreid62dpuwwlmnj2tqgbhpsnsmvchj6tfcetdqm2wu55zbuwm7zpacu"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:27:58.335Z",
			"content": "<p>Interop isn't Baseline; things that are in Interop are by definition not ready for Baseline, but having them as priorities in Interop means they might be in Baseline in a year or so; I wrote a couple of articles about this a while back</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23ifdmcc26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3ljzyjiprbk2d",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social/post/3lk23ifdmcc26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mary Branscombe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/bafkreid62dpuwwlmnj2tqgbhpsnsmvchj6tfcetdqm2wu55zbuwm7zpacu"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:32:53.750Z",
			"content": "<p>most granularity: going through the MDN pages individually for compat data on APIs and querying BCD<br>\nlots of granularity: caniuse against your own logs to see what your audience can benefit from<br>\nback of the envelope decisions about directions when you want to know what's mainstream: baseline</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23qudicc2q",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk237lmc2s26",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mdh2.bsky.social/post/3lk23qudicc2q",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:37:37.909Z",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23v3pq522q",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23qudicc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mdh2.bsky.social/post/3lk23v3pq522q",
