		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:hx35zjisxgynsrwdsrmj2egw/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk24j5k2p22q",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/ethanmarcotte.com/post/3lk24j5k2p22q",
			"author": {
				"name": "Ethan Marcotte",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/ethanmarcotte.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:hx35zjisxgynsrwdsrmj2egw/bafkreihkmjowfcdhyeupgbaartkthwghfbngo4uwghtjvjxj7kvl3hofoq"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T17:51:12.869Z",
			"content": "<p>oof, yeah. “baseline” doesn’t mean “universal”, and boy do i wish that informed we talk about these features</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk25wnfz5k2m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:hx35zjisxgynsrwdsrmj2egw/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk24j5k2p22q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com/post/3lk25wnfz5k2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian Kardell",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/bafkreiduzv2xwkhuudncicmqday73trtdnqedafwezzlojhio57wu4jhwi"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:16:39.463Z",
			"content": "<p>baseline widely available should mean something very close to that though - it's 30 months past the initial interoperability date, which we based on looking at gobs of data about rollouts.  Of course, all of these require nuance and weighing of your own users needs - but as a rule of thumb, p good?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk263snlcc2m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk25wnfz5k2m",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com/post/3lk263snlcc2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian Kardell",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/bafkreiduzv2xwkhuudncicmqday73trtdnqedafwezzlojhio57wu4jhwi"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:19:32.726Z",
			"content": "<p>Idk, iirc <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:widt5upyy6uevzv2n3ehtred\">@meyerweb.com</a> and I attempted to argue for something even more granular and with stages as numbers rather than words that could be more easily misread. There are a handful of 'stages' that are useful to identify.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk2674mbas2m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk263snlcc2m",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com/post/3lk2674mbas2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian Kardell",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/bafkreiduzv2xwkhuudncicmqday73trtdnqedafwezzlojhio57wu4jhwi"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:21:23.832Z",
			"content": "<p>For example, we made <a href=\"https://bcd-watch.igalia.com/weekly-completed/\">bcd-watch.igalia.com/weekly-compl...</a> which you can listen to a weekly rss feed of and it tells you when bcd records the final engine implementation.  That can be before it's even available in releases, but it's a very strong \"this is coming!\" - so probably worth your time</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk26lag3j22i",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:vcrxgrk7qttaunjut34oe5oq/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk22naoqcc2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lk26lag3j22i",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:28:10.477Z",
			"content": "<p>appreciate you Patrick! 🙌</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:hkqqtpy6cwwzkljkiexby6n6/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk26ww3j7c2k",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sassquad.net/post/3lk26ww3j7c2k",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stephen Scaaaaaaaaaaaaaght 😱",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sassquad.net",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:hkqqtpy6cwwzkljkiexby6n6/bafkreigyrun53skbr35pncxywmw5maxpann3cja5olokscdzwgvpt5d2de"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:34:42.296Z",
			"content": "<p>I thought of Baseline as a reference for us to tell stakeholders 'Yes, we can do this... but' in terms of enhanced clarity?</p>\n<p>Prior to Baseline, caniuse seems to be only alternative?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk27gvk7lc26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23qudicc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social/post/3lk27gvk7lc26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mary Branscombe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/marypcbuk.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/bafkreid62dpuwwlmnj2tqgbhpsnsmvchj6tfcetdqm2wu55zbuwm7zpacu"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:43:38.602Z",
			"content": "<p>Apple is a big part of why Interop happens (for both bad and good); it's at least moved things along from where they were before the annual Interop priority alignments - and no worries, I've been trying to explain how these fit together for a while and I'm about to have another go</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk27su62cs2m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xf7krjtyhvmoqjyl4dgiafey/app.bsky.feed.post/3lk23qudicc2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com/post/3lk27su62cs2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian Kardell",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bkardell.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:httl4meeb5mx5767hike2t4q/bafkreiduzv2xwkhuudncicmqday73trtdnqedafwezzlojhio57wu4jhwi"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-10T18:50:19.808Z",
			"content": "<p>Hi, I'd love to hear more (maybe not on this thread) about why you think interop 2025 is bad? Happy to use DMs or have a video chat or whatever you prefer</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
